doc1:works include ""The Life and Life-Work of Samuel Phelps"" (actor and theatre manager) as well as his own autobiography ""Johnston Forbes-Robertson: A Player Under Three Reigns"" (1925). On 6 November 1937 he died at St. Margaret's Bay, near Dover, Kent, and was cremated at Golders Green Crematorium, London on 9 November. Memorial services were held at St. Martin-in-the-Fields, Westminster, London. A statue of Forbes-Robertson by Brenda Putnam (1932) can be found at the Folger Shakespeare Library in Washington D.C.. Johnston Forbes-Robertson Sir Johnston Forbes-Robertson (16 January 1853 – 6 November 1937) was an English actor and theatre manager. He was
